Global component installation — 2026-10-16
Host: Darwin 24.6.0 x86_64, node v24.21.0, claude CLI 2.1.301
Decision: every component reaches the hosts through the global Apex install.

-- cc-safety-net 2.6.12
   Claude Code plugin, scope user, enabled. doctor: Detected/Configured/Verified.
   Test/test_safety_net.py runs against it and passes.

-- cc-sdd 3.1.0
   Not run per project. Its 17 skills are vendored under Claude/skills/ and
   install.py links each into ~/.claude/skills/. Its project-root CLAUDE.md and
   .kiro templates are deliberately not taken.
   Test/test_install.py asserts the links are made and removed again.

-- tdd-guard (plugin 1.3.0, wrapping npx tdd-guard@latest)
   Claude Code plugin, scope user, enabled everywhere at the user's instruction.

   OPEN RISK, measured here, not resolved:
   A real edit in this repository was put to the guard and came back
     {"decision":"block","reason":"Error during validation: Not logged in · Please run /login"}
   The refusal is not a TDD judgement. The guard could not reach a model, and it
   fails closed, so it denied the edit. A 'Claude Code-credentials' keychain entry
   exists, so an authenticated desktop session may well succeed; this sandboxed
   shell cannot read the keychain and so cannot prove it either way.

   If code edits start being refused with a login message, turn it off by sending
   'tdd-guard off' as a message, or remove it with:
     claude plugin disable tdd-guard@tdd-guard

   Second limit: this repository's suite is unittest, and tdd-guard ships reporters
   for vitest, jest, storybook and pytest. Without a reporter it has no test results
   to reason about, so its judgement here rests on the diff alone.
